  },
  "sourceLocator": {
    "chapter": "Magic Items",
    "section": "10.4",
    "heading": "Potions",
    "lineStart": 14593,
    "lineEnd": 14602
  },
  "columns": [
    "1d100",
    "Result"
  ],
  "rows": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "cells": [
        {
          "value": "01"
        },
        {
          "value": "Both potions lose their effects, and the mixture creates a magical explosion in a 5-foot-radius Sphere centered on itself. Each creature in that area takes 4d10 Force damage."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "cells": [
        {
          "value": "02–08"
        },
        {
          "value": "Both potions lose their effects, and the mixture becomes an ingested poison of your choice (see “Poison” in “Gameplay Toolbox”)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "cells": [
        {
          "value": "09–15"
        },
        {
          "value": "Both potions lose their effects."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "cells": [
        {
          "value": "16–25"
        },
        {
          "value": "One potion loses its effect."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "cells": [
        {
          "value": "26–35"
        },
        {
          "value": "Both potions work, but with their numerical effects and durations halved. If a potion has no numerical effect and no duration, it instead loses its effect."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "cells": [
        {
          "value": "36–90"
        },
        {
          "value": "Both potions work normally."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "cells": [
        {
          "value": "91–99"
        },
        {
          "value": "Both potions work, but the numerical effects and duration of one potion are doubled. If neither potion has anything to double in this way, they work normally."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "position": 8,
      "cells": [
        {
          "value": "00"
        },
        {
          "value": "Only one potion works, but its effects are permanent. Choose the simplest effect to make permanent or the one that seems the most fun. For example, a Potion of Healing might increase the drinker’s Hit Point maximum by 2d4 + 2, or a Potion of Invisibility might give the drinker the Invisible condition indefinitely. At your discretion, a Dispel Magic spell or similar magic might end this lasting effect."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "rawText": "| 1d100 | Result                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               |\n| :---- | :------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 01    | Both potions lose their effects, and the mixture creates a magical explosion in a 5-foot-radius Sphere centered on itself. Each creature in that area takes 4d10 Force damage.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| 02–08 | Both potions lose their effects, and the mixture becomes an ingested poison of your choice (see “Poison” in “Gameplay Toolbox”).                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| 09–15 | Both potions lose their effects.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| 16–25 | One potion loses its effect.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |\n| 26–35 | Both potions work, but with their numerical effects and durations halved. If a potion has no numerical effect and no duration, it instead loses its effect.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n| 36–90 | Both potions work normally.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n| 91–99 | Both potions work, but the numerical effects and duration of one potion are doubled. If neither potion has anything to double in this way, they work normally.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| 00    | Only one potion works, but its effects are permanent. Choose the simplest effect to make permanent or the one that seems the most fun. For example, a Potion of Healing might increase the drinker’s Hit Point maximum by 2d4 + 2, or a Potion of Invisibility might give the drinker the Invisible condition indefinitely. At your discretion, a Dispel Magic spell or similar magic might end this lasting effect. |"
